# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the ant_uv suite.
#
# druntime's garbage collector stops the world with a signal; its handler is
# reported for spoiling errno when it interrupts the loop thread inside
# epoll_wait. That is a runtime matter (the fork-join lane suppresses the
# same report), not a loop race. libuv itself is deliberately not
# suppressed: suppressing calls from it would also hide its mutexes, which
# carry the happens-before edges from its auxiliary threads.
signal:thread_suspendHandler
#
# druntime is not instrumented, so TSan cannot see the GC's lock but does see
# the libc memset the allocator calls when it clears large blocks. Worker
# Fibers allocating large buffers concurrently therefore report a race whose
# both sides are inside the conservative GC's allocator. Only frames of that
# implementation match this pattern.
race:_D4core8internal2gc4impl12conservative
